169	\section{Experimental Setup}
170	
171	\paragraph{Controlled Contamination Injection.}
172	We fine-tune Qwen2.5 models at four scales (0.5B, 1.5B, 3B, 7B) using LoRA SFT at four contamination dosage levels: d000 (clean), d005 (5\% items contaminated), d025 (25\%), d100 (100\%).
173	Each condition is run with 2--3 random seeds.
174	Multi-seed pooling yields $N_{\text{models}} \geq 32$.
175	
176	\paragraph{Benchmarks.}
177	MMLU (1,000 items subsampled), ARC-Challenge (1,172 items), GSM8K (1,319 items; negative control---open-ended format resists contamination), and HumanEval (164 items; appendix only).
178	
179	\paragraph{Baselines (7).}
180	(0)~Raw scores, (1)~Remove-and-rescore, (2)~Single-signal 2PL+$\gamma$, (3)~Vanilla 4PL ($\gamma{=}0$), (4)~Linear exposure regression, (5)~Emperor mitigation strategies \citep{oren2024proving}, (6)~DCR \citep{yang2025dcr}.
181	
182	\paragraph{Evaluation Metrics (6).}
183	MAE (pp), 95\%/80\%/50\% credible interval coverage, CI sharpness (width), Kendall's $\tau$, dose-response monotonicity, and SBC diagnostic \citep{talts2020validating}.
